# Architecture Standards

## Layers
Presentation → Application → Infrastructure

- Application owns business logic; zero infrastructure dependencies
- Infrastructure implements interfaces from Application
- Presentation depends on Application only

## Structure
- Application: Features (vertical slices), Common (Interfaces, Behaviors, Models)
- Infrastructure: Persistence (EF Core, Repositories), Services
- Presentation: Endpoints

## SOLID
- SRP: one reason to change
- OCP: extend, don't modify
- LSP: subtypes substitutable
- ISP: small, role-specific interfaces
- DIP: Application defines; Infrastructure implements

## Models
Private setters; factory methods; encapsulate invariants

## Do
Business logic in Application; interfaces in Application; Value Objects for Money, Email

## Don't
Infrastructure refs in Application; business logic in endpoints; async void
